  "problem": {
    "id": "train-5996",
    "question": "An apple tree produces 40 apples in its first year.  The second year the apple tree produces 8 more than double the amount of apples that it produced the first year, and the third year production went down by a fourth due to an insect infestation.  How many apples did the tree produce in total in the first three years?",
    "gold": "194",
    "answer": "First Year:40 apples\nSecond Year:8+2(40)=88 apples\nThird year:88-88/4=<<88-88/4=66>>66 apples\nTotal 40+88+66=<<40+88+66=194>>194 apples\n#### 194"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total number of apples produced by the apple tree over the first three years, we will calculate the production for each year step by step.\n\n1. **First Year Production:**\n   The apple tree produces 40 apples in its first year.\n   \\[\n   \\text{First year production} = 40\n   \\]\n\n2. **Second Year Production:**\n   The second year production is 8 more than double the amount produced in the first year. First, we calculate double the first year production:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 40 = 80\n   \\]\n   Then, we add 8 to this amount to find the second year production:\n   \\[\n   80 + 8 = 88\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Second year production} = 88\n   \\]\n\n3. **Third Year Production:**\n   The third year production is one-fourth of the second year production. First, we calculate one-fourth of the second year production:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{88}{4} = 22\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Third year production} = 22\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total Production Over Three Years:**\n   To find the total number of apples produced over the first three years, we sum the production from each year:\n   \\[\n   40 + 88 + 22 = 150\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of apples produced by the tree in the first three years is \\(\\boxed{150}\\).",
